 For fixed `r`, UHTE is finite: the rhombus normal set is fixed, global equality
 spaces are cut out by subsets of that set, and every intrinsic face normal
 cone is generated by restrictions of those normals.  A weaker sufficient
 version may replace the standard Berline--Vergne weights by any coherent
 McMullen local formula that is nonnegative on precisely these realized cones.
+
+### Correction: the actual quotient frontier
+
+Raw componentwise nonnegativity of the Berline--Vergne vector `alpha` is only
+a strong sufficient condition.  It is not used by the rank-4 certificate.
+For a fixed rank and face dimension, let `S` be the rational span of the
+actual hive face-volume vectors `Lambda(H)`, after imposing the balancing
+(equivalently, Chow) relations.  The required statement is the existence of
+a componentwise nonnegative stencil `mu` such that
+
+```
+Lambda(H) dot mu = Lambda(H) dot alpha
+```
+
+for every hive `H`, equivalently `mu-alpha` annihilates `S`.  The rank-4 proof
+constructs exactly such a representative on its edge-volume quotient even
+though it never proves `alpha >= 0`.  A rank-uniform construction of these
+nonnegative quotient representatives, for every intermediate face dimension,
+is the real full-KTT frontier.
+
+There can be no generic braid-fan or permutohedral effectivity theorem of this
+kind.  Castillo--Liu, *On the Todd Class of the Permutohedral Variety*,
+arXiv:1909.09127, Theorem 6.4, proves that the Todd class of the
+permutohedral variety `X_d` is not effective for every `d >= 24`.  Thus any
+uniform result must use restrictions special to realized hive face-volume
+data rather than positivity of the ambient fan's raw Todd weights.
